# ── Mobile reference app ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development only. Staging and production values live in Infisical and
# are injected at build time (Section 12).
#
# NOTE: everything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the app bundle and is
# readable by anyone who downloads it. Only publishable, non-secret values
# belong here.
#
# There is deliberately no DATABASE_URL. Unlike core-web, this app holds no
# database connection of any kind — not to core, and not to a schema of its own.
# Every fact about identity, organisation and permissions arrives through the
# Core API (Sections 1.3 and 5.5).

# ── Clerk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave unset to run with the development stand-in. Setting a real publishable
# key switches authentication to Clerk with no code change.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
#
# There is no secret key here, and there cannot be one. core-web carries
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY server-side where the browser never sees it; this app has no
# server side, so the publishable key is the only Clerk credential it can hold.

# ── Google and Microsoft sign-in ────────────────────────────────────────
# There are deliberately no OAuth variables here.
#
# Google and Microsoft client IDs and secrets are entered in the CLERK
# DASHBOARD, per provider, per instance. Clerk performs the OAuth handshake and
# this app never holds or sees those credentials.
#
# The mobile difference is where the handshake returns to: the system browser
# hands control back through this app's custom scheme (`beorchidcore`, set in
# app.json), not through a redirect URL configured here (Section 4.4).
#
# Setup steps: core-api/docs/clerk-configuration.md

# ── Core API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately unset. Absence selects StubCoreClient, which serves the same
# interface from a fixture.
#
# Your machine's LAN address, NOT localhost — a phone or simulator resolves
# localhost to itself, not to the host running Core API.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CORE_API_URL=http://192.168.1.50:3000
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CORE_API_KEY does not exist and must never be added.
# core-web keeps CORE_API_KEY server-side; a mobile bundle has nowhere to keep
# a shared secret, so shipping one would hand every person who downloads the
# app a credential that reads any user in the system.
#
# How mobile authenticates to Core API instead: every request carries the
# signed-in user's OWN Clerk session token (Authorization: Bearer <clerk-jwt>),
# obtained through the existing session seam and sent by UserTokenCoreClient
# (src/lib/core.ts). Core API verifies that token itself against Clerk's JWKS
# and resolves the calling app to core_mobile server-side — see
# core-api/src/middleware/clerk-auth.ts and core-api/src/routes/mobile.ts.
#
# Setting this URL therefore requires EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY to be
# set too: without a real Clerk session there is no token to present, and
# src/lib/core.ts refuses that combination outright rather than silently
# sending an unauthenticated request.
#
# core_mobile must also be registered in core.apps before this resolves to
# anything but a 503 — see core-api/docs/registering-core-mobile.md.
